I built and saved the main-B agent from Brief A and Brief B. One chat turn shows it starts: it said "Hello, I am Freya Bank's digital assistant and this call is recorded. Am I speaking with Ms Lee?" I ran no practice cases (as instructed), and I did not do the final rule-by-rule re-read of the brief because of the time limit. Lint shows 0 errors and the situations check lists no problems.

- **Call flow:** the date-facts code node from `main-B.calc.json` is the start node, unedited. The call then goes opening → identity → account lookup → router → negotiate, and ends in a goodbye node. The account lookup runs `get_account` with the hook from the same file, verbatim.
- **Specialist nodes:** hardship, dispute, already_paid, cannot_pay_transfer, callback and no_callback, each with only its own rules and tools.
- **Where it differs from the extracted situations:**
  - The brief says a dispute or "already paid" about one product does not end the call (Brief B rule 9). So in negotiate the agent notes that product and carries on with the others. It only moves to the dispute or already_paid node when the claim covers all the remaining products.
  - Brief B says to add no notes on any transfer, so the hardship node adds no notes when the customer accepts the transfer to support.
- **Other notes:** I put the two brief rules that no code step computes into the prompts in the brief's own words: date-of-birth format in identity, and one date for all products in negotiate. The generator is `out/main-B.gen.py`.

